          "text": "The reflections index on an **F-centered cubic cell** with \\(a \\approx 8.289\\) \u00c5. For example, the first five peaks are 111, 200, 220, 311, and 222. The missing/very weak 400 and 620 reflections rule out ordinary monatomic fcc Ga. The best assignment is a **cF32 cubic Ga allotrope**, space group \\(F\\overline{4}3m\\) (No. 216), with two Ga 16e sites.\n\n```cif\ndata_Ga_cF32\n_audit_creation_method              'Indexed and fitted from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common               'cubic gallium, cF32 model'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Ga'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               32\n\n_cell_length_a                      8.2890\n_cell_length_b                      8.2890\n_cell_length_c                      8.2890\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   90\n_cell_volume                        569.52\n\n_space_group_crystal_system         cubic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'F -4 3 m'\n_space_group_IT_number              216\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn       6.51\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nGa1  Ga  16  e  0.1040  0.1040  0.1040  1.0  0.010\nGa2  Ga  16  e  0.2700  0.2700  0.2700  1.0  0.010\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing:\n\n| \\(hkl\\) | Calculated \\(2\\theta\\) | Observed \\(2\\theta\\) |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 111 | 18.53\u00b0 | 18.53\u00b0 |\n| 200 | 21.42\u00b0 | 21.42\u00b0 |\n| 220 | 30.48\u00b0 | 30.48\u00b0 |\n| 311 | 35.90\u00b0 | 35.90\u00b0 |\n| 222 | 37.56\u00b0 | 37.56\u00b0 |\n| 331 | 47.79\u00b0 | 47.79\u00b0 |\n| 420 | 49.12\u00b0 | 49.12\u00b0 |\n| 422 | 54.16\u00b0 | 54.16\u00b0 |\n| 511/333 | 57.74\u00b0 | 57.74\u00b0